1
00:01:35,799 --> 00:01:37,959
Publicity Dept, Hongye City Public Security Bureau, Zhongjiang Province

2
00:01:38,200 --> 00:01:39,239
jointly with the SWAT Detachment

3
00:01:39,359 --> 00:01:40,840
hosted a Police Open Day event.

4
00:01:41,560 --> 00:01:42,719
Citizens of Hongye at the scene

5
00:01:42,719 --> 00:01:44,439
immersed themselves in police culture.

6
00:01:45,000 --> 00:01:46,200
The SWAT members demonstrated

7
00:01:46,200 --> 00:01:47,599
Let's not post this video for now.

8
00:01:47,959 --> 00:01:49,079
the combined use of batons and shields.

9
00:01:49,079 --> 00:01:49,439
Director Tan,

10
00:01:49,680 --> 00:01:51,040
is there something wrong with my editing?

11
00:01:51,040 --> 00:01:51,920
The SWAT members' grappling and combat skills

12
00:01:51,920 --> 00:01:52,920
Your editing is fine.

13
00:01:53,840 --> 00:01:54,920
won rounds of applause.

14
00:01:55,079 --> 00:01:56,439
Then shouldn't we tell Chief Zhao

15
00:01:56,439 --> 00:01:57,280
about this?

16
00:01:57,280 --> 00:02:00,040
Holding six Police Open Day events over three years,

17
00:02:00,560 --> 00:02:02,239
the safety knowledge awareness rate among local residents

18
00:02:02,239 --> 00:02:04,040
has increased by 40%.

19
00:02:04,799 --> 00:02:05,920
Through role-playing experiences,

20
00:02:05,920 --> 00:02:07,359
the proper emergency reporting awareness formed

21
00:02:07,719 --> 00:02:09,199
has also played an effective role

22
00:02:09,280 --> 00:02:10,120
in multiple emergencies.

23
00:02:11,199 --> 00:02:11,960
Hongye Police

24
00:02:11,960 --> 00:02:14,039
will deepen the Police-School Cooperation Mechanism,

25
00:02:14,599 --> 00:02:17,080
using the regular spring and autumn openings as a pivot,

26
00:02:17,719 --> 00:02:19,319
to innovate forms of legal education,

27
00:02:19,520 --> 00:02:21,479
making police guardrails where authority and warmth coexist

28
00:02:21,479 --> 00:02:22,039
Chief Zhao.

29
00:02:22,159 --> 00:02:23,639
the most beautiful backdrop for their growth.

30
00:02:23,879 --> 00:02:26,439
That Police Open Day video,

31
00:02:27,240 --> 00:02:28,120
let's not post it for now.

32
00:02:30,520 --> 00:02:31,560
You decide on this, Director Tan.

33
00:02:32,520 --> 00:02:33,680
You're the lead deputy director.

34
00:02:35,639 --> 00:02:36,360
Then we won't post it.

35
00:02:37,080 --> 00:02:39,639
I... I found a standard obituary.

36
00:02:41,159 --> 00:02:43,759
But it's a template for a senior comrade who died of illness.

37
00:02:44,919 --> 00:02:45,560
And Lu Zhong...

38
00:02:46,159 --> 00:02:47,280
died in the line of duty.

39
00:02:49,719 --> 00:02:50,400
Let me see.

40
00:02:55,199 --> 00:02:55,599
Lu Zhong...

41
00:02:55,879 --> 00:02:57,120
Was Lu Zhong even 40 yet?

42
00:02:57,960 --> 00:02:58,840
41.

43
00:03:03,360 --> 00:03:06,120
Then across our entire system nationwide every year,

44
00:03:07,479 --> 00:03:08,400
how many families must

45
00:03:09,520 --> 00:03:10,599
go through this kind of pain?

46
00:04:05,080 --> 00:04:05,800
Comrade Shaoping,

47
00:04:07,240 --> 00:04:09,120
the passing of your husband, Comrade Lu Zhong,

48
00:04:10,800 --> 00:04:13,000
is a tremendous loss to our force.

49
00:04:14,599 --> 00:04:15,439
Just like you,

50
00:04:17,759 --> 00:04:20,759
we are all deeply heartbroken and devastated.

51
00:04:22,160 --> 00:04:22,720
Today,

52
00:04:23,079 --> 00:04:25,240
the bureau's leadership team and I,

53
00:04:26,000 --> 00:04:27,800
along with Comrade Lu Zhong's fellow officers,

54
00:04:28,160 --> 00:04:28,759
have come to your home.

55
00:04:31,160 --> 00:04:32,680
First, to express our deepest condolences.

56
00:04:34,360 --> 00:04:35,079
And secondly,

57
00:04:36,079 --> 00:04:36,759
this is also a token of support

58
00:04:36,759 --> 00:04:38,279
from all of his fellow officers.

59
00:04:40,079 --> 00:04:40,800
Please accept it.

60
00:04:50,160 --> 00:04:51,240
Thank you, Chief.

61
00:04:54,079 --> 00:04:56,439
If you face any difficulties at all,

62
00:04:57,319 --> 00:04:58,519
reach out to the department anytime.

63
00:05:06,160 --> 00:05:06,720
Thank you.

64
00:05:09,319 --> 00:05:10,839
I appreciate everyone's concern.

65
00:05:13,160 --> 00:05:14,120
You should all head back.

66
00:05:15,399 --> 00:05:16,360
You're all very busy.

67
00:05:27,800 --> 00:05:28,120
Okay.

68
00:05:47,160 --> 00:05:47,680
No need to see us out.

69
00:06:24,519 --> 00:06:26,600
Our station was supposed to respond yesterday,

70
00:06:27,319 --> 00:06:28,519
but since we were short-staffed,

71
00:06:28,839 --> 00:06:30,439
I requested backup from our superiors.

72
00:06:33,439 --> 00:06:34,439
If we had all been there,

73
00:06:34,519 --> 00:06:35,759
nothing would have happened to Commissar Lu.

74
00:06:36,720 --> 00:06:37,800
Regarding Lu Zhong's sacrifice,

75
00:06:38,759 --> 00:06:39,759
I bear some responsibility too.

76
00:06:40,959 --> 00:06:42,879
As for the SWAT team, I was the one

77
00:06:43,279 --> 00:06:44,959
who suggested they attend the investment conference.

78
00:06:58,439 --> 00:06:59,360
Losing a comrade

79
00:07:00,000 --> 00:07:02,480
is painful, of course.

80
00:07:05,120 --> 00:07:06,040
But after the grief,

81
00:07:06,800 --> 00:07:07,800
what's important is

82
00:07:08,680 --> 00:07:10,360
to keep our emotions in check

83
00:07:11,279 --> 00:07:12,319
and analyze the situation.

84
00:07:14,480 --> 00:07:15,519
My analysis

85
00:07:15,720 --> 00:07:16,920
is that this incident

86
00:07:16,920 --> 00:07:19,680
was caused by incomplete intelligence gathering.

87
00:07:20,639 --> 00:07:21,519
We underestimated them.

88
00:07:21,800 --> 00:07:23,279
Thought it was just a gambling ring.

89
00:07:24,920 --> 00:07:25,639
He's already gone.

90
00:07:26,600 --> 00:07:27,480
Is there any point in saying this now?

91
00:07:28,560 --> 00:07:29,360
Of course there is.

92
00:07:31,639 --> 00:07:32,519
Doesn't all valuable experience

93
00:07:32,519 --> 00:07:34,519
come from painful lessons?

94
00:07:37,079 --> 00:07:38,000
Don't you agree?

95
00:07:45,800 --> 00:07:46,560
Just eat your noodles.

96
00:07:46,560 --> 00:07:46,920
They'll get soggy.

97
00:08:23,720 --> 00:08:24,920
These tomatoes are really good.

98
00:08:25,279 --> 00:08:27,040
They're good because, bit by bit,

99
00:08:27,040 --> 00:08:27,680
I put in the work.

100
00:08:38,879 --> 00:08:40,480
Today, let's set a small goal.

101
00:08:41,200 --> 00:08:42,360
For this year's provincial competition,

102
00:08:42,480 --> 00:08:43,360
at the very, very least,

103
00:08:43,639 --> 00:08:44,519
we'll take first place in the province.

104
00:08:44,720 --> 00:08:45,240
It's settled.

105
00:08:47,639 --> 00:08:49,080
Imagine if one day,

106
00:08:49,200 --> 00:08:50,399
we could stand on that podium too.

107
00:08:50,960 --> 00:08:51,639
How would that feel?

108
00:08:52,399 --> 00:08:53,480
Sometimes I think about it so much

109
00:08:53,960 --> 00:08:54,480
that I just fall asleep.

110
00:08:55,240 --> 00:08:55,600
Not gonna lie,

111
00:08:56,960 --> 00:08:58,279
you can have anything in your dreams.

112
00:10:10,159 --> 00:10:10,679
Let's just sleep.

113
00:10:15,000 --> 00:10:15,879
You can have it all in your dreams.

114
00:10:45,360 --> 00:10:45,799
Sir,

115
00:10:45,919 --> 00:10:46,480
take your time.

116
00:10:46,559 --> 00:10:47,600
Take your time and speak clearly.

117
00:10:48,000 --> 00:10:48,879
Roughly where was it?

118
00:10:49,279 --> 00:10:50,519
I had just left my house,

119
00:10:50,679 --> 00:10:51,440
going for a walk.

120
00:10:51,960 --> 00:10:53,919
Then I saw those kids over here holding...

121
00:10:54,519 --> 00:10:54,799
Chief Ji.

122
00:10:55,080 --> 00:10:55,840
This gentleman called the police.

123
00:10:57,399 --> 00:10:57,799
That was me.

124
00:10:58,120 --> 00:10:58,840
Here's what happened.

125
00:10:59,519 --> 00:10:59,879
Go ahead.

126
00:10:59,960 --> 00:11:00,440
I was

127
00:11:00,639 --> 00:11:01,440
taking a walk,

128
00:11:01,840 --> 00:11:02,799
when I saw those kids

129
00:11:03,120 --> 00:11:04,120
playing with this thing.

130
00:11:04,919 --> 00:11:06,120
I noticed something was off,

131
00:11:06,559 --> 00:11:07,200
so I grabbed it

132
00:11:07,200 --> 00:11:08,559
and weighed it in my hands.

133
00:11:09,080 --> 00:11:09,759
It's solid iron.

134
00:11:10,600 --> 00:11:11,000
A real gun.

135
00:11:13,200 --> 00:11:13,519
Chief.

136
00:11:14,360 --> 00:11:14,720
This is him.

137
00:11:16,720 --> 00:11:18,399
Kid, did you find this?

138
00:11:19,440 --> 00:11:20,240
Where did you find it?

139
00:11:20,600 --> 00:11:22,600
I found it behind that tree.

140
00:11:33,000 --> 00:11:33,600
We can confirm

141
00:11:33,840 --> 00:11:34,679
this homemade gun

142
00:11:34,679 --> 00:11:36,039
is the weapon that killed Lu Zhong.

143
00:11:36,519 --> 00:11:38,159
We lifted several fingerprints from it.

144
00:11:40,360 --> 00:11:42,440
Excluding the kids who found the gun,

145
00:11:42,840 --> 00:11:43,639
there are two other fingerprints left.

146
00:11:44,720 --> 00:11:45,600
After running them through the database,

147
00:11:45,639 --> 00:11:46,399
one of them

148
00:11:47,120 --> 00:11:48,759
matched the suspect Jin Yonggang.

149
00:11:50,159 --> 00:11:50,879
What about the other one?

150
00:11:53,360 --> 00:11:54,240
No match was found.

151
00:12:18,600 --> 00:12:19,840
Hello? Who is it?

152
00:12:20,679 --> 00:12:22,600
Mr. Jin, this is Xiaomin.

153
00:12:23,840 --> 00:12:24,480
Oh, Xiaomin.

154
00:12:24,919 --> 00:12:25,759
What can I do for you?

155
00:12:26,799 --> 00:12:28,200
Sister Liu from the neighborhood committee said

156
00:12:28,399 --> 00:12:29,519
she has some rice for you,

157
00:12:29,840 --> 00:12:30,879
and she asked me to bring it over.

158
00:12:31,200 --> 00:12:32,200
I can't carry it by myself.

159
00:12:32,600 --> 00:12:34,000
Um, is Gangzi home?

160
00:12:34,039 --> 00:12:35,639
Yes, yes, he's here.

161
00:12:35,840 --> 00:12:36,879
I'll have him carry it in a bit.

162
00:12:37,960 --> 00:12:39,360
Okay, see you in a bit, Mr. Jin.

163
00:12:40,200 --> 00:12:41,399
Okay, bye.

164
00:12:44,320 --> 00:12:44,720
Gangzi!

165
00:13:00,399 --> 00:13:00,799
Chief Guo,

166
00:13:01,519 --> 00:13:02,360
The SWAT team is in position.

167
00:13:02,799 --> 00:13:03,679
Ready to breach at any time.

168
00:13:04,600 --> 00:13:04,960
Here's the plan.

169
00:13:05,639 --> 00:13:06,360
As soon as the door opens,

170
00:13:07,240 --> 00:13:08,120
leave the rest

171
00:13:08,399 --> 00:13:09,679
to Liao Bufan and Lao Na.

172
00:13:10,360 --> 00:13:11,200
You must be careful.

173
00:13:12,159 --> 00:13:14,360
Jin Yonggang might still have a gun.

174
00:13:15,039 --> 00:13:16,279
You must ensure everyone's safety.

175
00:13:16,720 --> 00:13:16,879
Yes, sir.

176
00:13:17,120 --> 00:13:17,360
Understood.

177
00:13:19,000 --> 00:13:19,440
Chief Guo,

178
00:13:20,159 --> 00:13:21,799
the old man isn't doing well mentally.

179
00:13:22,360 --> 00:13:23,039
He gets frightened easily.

180
00:13:24,039 --> 00:13:25,759
Could you let me go in first?

181
00:13:26,080 --> 00:13:26,440
Chief Guo,

182
00:13:27,360 --> 00:13:28,399
the target is highly dangerous.

183
00:13:28,720 --> 00:13:30,039
We can't guarantee her safety.

184
00:13:30,440 --> 00:13:31,399
It's safer to breach.

185
00:13:31,519 --> 00:13:32,399
This is my jurisdiction.

186
00:13:32,879 --> 00:13:34,320
I know Jin Yonggang's family situation best.

187
00:13:35,000 --> 00:13:36,399
I'm confident I can persuade him.

188
00:13:38,279 --> 00:13:38,559
Fair enough.

189
00:13:39,759 --> 00:13:40,639
Choose your moment carefully.

190
00:13:41,360 --> 00:13:43,679
You two follow closely behind her.

191
00:13:43,960 --> 00:13:44,879
If anything goes wrong,

192
00:13:45,320 --> 00:13:45,919
breach immediately.

193
00:13:46,080 --> 00:13:46,519
Yes, sir.

194
00:13:49,519 --> 00:13:50,000
Thank you, Chief Guo.

195
00:13:53,639 --> 00:13:54,240
Put this on.

196
00:13:56,720 --> 00:13:57,039
No need.

197
00:13:57,639 --> 00:13:58,000
Wait,

198
00:14:00,320 --> 00:14:00,559
you...

199
00:14:01,840 --> 00:14:02,240
Go on, hurry.

200
00:14:36,679 --> 00:14:37,480
Mr. Jin

201
00:14:52,159 --> 00:14:52,960
Mr. Jin.

202
00:14:57,919 --> 00:14:58,600
Mr. Jin.

203
00:14:58,919 --> 00:14:59,840
It's Xiaomin.

204
00:15:18,200 --> 00:15:18,919
Mr. Jin

205
00:16:01,320 --> 00:16:01,639
You...

206
00:16:02,879 --> 00:16:03,360
Xiaomin...

207
00:16:04,600 --> 00:16:06,440
Did Gangzi get into trouble again?

208
00:17:52,640 --> 00:17:53,440
We can't stay here anymore.

209
00:18:22,240 --> 00:18:23,119
Unlocked.

210
00:18:23,920 --> 00:18:24,519
You're back.

211
00:18:28,000 --> 00:18:28,599
Did you eat?

212
00:18:29,599 --> 00:18:30,079
Not yet.

213
00:18:30,880 --> 00:18:31,640
I've got everything ready.

214
00:18:32,799 --> 00:18:33,200
It'll just be a minute.

215
00:18:35,319 --> 00:18:36,079
I heard about it.

216
00:18:37,039 --> 00:18:38,319
They're searching the nearby neighborhoods.

217
00:18:38,960 --> 00:18:40,519
Doing a grid search, going door-to-door.

218
00:18:51,160 --> 00:18:51,680
Where is he?

219
00:18:55,920 --> 00:18:56,759
Boiling water for the dumplings.

220
00:19:12,240 --> 00:19:13,759
Don't be so tense.

221
00:19:13,960 --> 00:19:15,640
A case this big takes time.

222
00:19:21,160 --> 00:19:23,160
They found out who killed Lu Zhong.

223
00:19:24,359 --> 00:19:25,039
It's Jin Yonggang.

224
00:19:31,559 --> 00:19:32,440
Did they catch him?

225
00:19:35,079 --> 00:19:35,559
They went after him.

226
00:19:36,400 --> 00:19:37,039
He wasn't home.

227
00:19:41,240 --> 00:19:41,960
Did CID go?

228
00:19:42,480 --> 00:19:43,119
They all went.

229
00:19:50,039 --> 00:19:51,160
For such a major incident,

230
00:19:51,319 --> 00:19:52,440
why didn't Lao Na tell me?

231
00:19:58,640 --> 00:20:00,200
Given what's happening with Mr. Jin's family,

232
00:20:00,319 --> 00:20:01,279
you should stay away for now.

233
00:20:01,920 --> 00:20:02,599
Best not to run into them.

234
00:20:06,039 --> 00:20:06,839
Gangzi committed the crime.

235
00:20:06,960 --> 00:20:08,039
What does it have to do with Mr. Jin?

236
00:20:08,720 --> 00:20:09,880
It's a highly sensitive time.

237
00:20:10,079 --> 00:20:11,119
It wouldn't look good for you.

238
00:20:18,559 --> 00:20:20,160
Mackerel dumplings. Should I boil them?

239
00:20:20,400 --> 00:20:21,119
I have no appetite.

240
00:20:33,480 --> 00:20:34,079
Next.

241
00:20:35,279 --> 00:20:35,880
Wang Yunsheng, step up.

242
00:20:36,759 --> 00:20:36,960
Step up.

243
00:20:41,440 --> 00:20:42,599
Next, step up.

244
00:20:53,480 --> 00:20:54,480
Who else? Come on!

245
00:20:54,720 --> 00:20:56,359
Did none of you eat today?

246
00:20:56,359 --> 00:20:57,160
Come on, come on!

247
00:20:57,160 --> 00:20:58,240
Come at me together! Come on! Come on!

248
00:20:58,240 --> 00:20:58,400
Come on!

249
00:20:59,839 --> 00:21:01,000
What's got Captain Liao so pissed off?

250
00:21:30,839 --> 00:21:31,519
Are you okay, Captain Liao?

251
00:21:44,160 --> 00:21:45,400
When I said this is absolutely unacceptable,

252
00:21:45,400 --> 00:21:46,440
I wasn't being an alarmist.

253
00:21:47,000 --> 00:21:47,640
Do you understand, comrades?

254
00:21:48,480 --> 00:21:49,759
If these drugs

255
00:21:50,200 --> 00:21:51,640
are confirmed to be here in Hongye,

256
00:21:52,200 --> 00:21:53,640
the responsibility we'll bear in the future

257
00:21:53,880 --> 00:21:55,240
is unimaginable.

258
00:21:56,599 --> 00:21:57,279
Why isn't Lin Nan here yet?

259
00:21:57,799 --> 00:21:58,720
Call Captain Lin.

260
00:21:58,960 --> 00:21:59,559
I'll ask him where he is.

261
00:21:59,680 --> 00:22:00,319
I'll call him.

262
00:22:02,559 --> 00:22:03,319
Think about it.

263
00:22:04,279 --> 00:22:05,440
If these drugs came here,

264
00:22:07,359 --> 00:22:08,759
what does it mean for us?

265
00:22:08,759 --> 00:22:09,480
What did you hear?

266
00:22:12,000 --> 00:22:12,920
You startled me!

267
00:22:12,920 --> 00:22:14,119
It means trouble is coming.

268
00:22:14,440 --> 00:22:17,240
Chief Guo sounds really upset.

269
00:22:18,119 --> 00:22:19,039
He called your name.

270
00:22:19,599 --> 00:22:20,759
Be careful when you go in.

271
00:22:23,200 --> 00:22:24,079
Why aren't you going in?

272
00:22:25,200 --> 00:22:25,960
He didn't call my name.

273
00:22:29,359 --> 00:22:30,119
We'll do the specific work.

274
00:22:30,880 --> 00:22:31,240
Chief Guo,

275
00:22:32,359 --> 00:22:33,640
Tan Yan says he has something to report.

276
00:22:34,000 --> 00:22:34,640
Tell him to hurry up.

277
00:22:36,039 --> 00:22:36,279
No,

278
00:22:36,279 --> 00:22:36,680
Tan Yan,

279
00:22:37,079 --> 00:22:38,200
wait outside for a moment.

280
00:22:42,079 --> 00:22:42,880
We've been waiting for you,

281
00:22:48,279 --> 00:22:48,720
Lin Nan.

282
00:22:50,000 --> 00:22:50,680
Starting now,

283
00:22:51,519 --> 00:22:54,039
the Economic Crime Investigation Unit officially joins the Task Force.

284
00:22:54,640 --> 00:22:54,920
Yes, sir.

285
00:22:55,160 --> 00:22:55,880
Your primary task

286
00:22:56,799 --> 00:22:58,799
is to check this Lang Tao's accounts first.

287
00:22:59,480 --> 00:23:00,480
Logically speaking,

288
00:23:01,799 --> 00:23:02,519
where there are drugs,

289
00:23:03,720 --> 00:23:05,319
there must be a massive amount of drug money.

290
00:23:06,839 --> 00:23:07,799
Who sent this money,

291
00:23:08,799 --> 00:23:10,319
and where did he send it?

292
00:23:11,279 --> 00:23:13,720
Is it a single-line or multi-directional flow?

293
00:23:14,480 --> 00:23:15,640
From the source to the destination,

294
00:23:16,079 --> 00:23:17,440
every transaction must be investigated thoroughly.

295
00:23:17,640 --> 00:23:18,119
Get to the bottom of it.

296
00:23:19,000 --> 00:23:19,279
Understood.

297
00:23:20,000 --> 00:23:20,279
Chief Guo,

298
00:23:21,319 --> 00:23:22,640
here is our current plan.

299
00:23:23,279 --> 00:23:23,920
We plan to

300
00:23:24,279 --> 00:23:26,799
collaborate with banks and payment platforms.

301
00:23:27,799 --> 00:23:28,839
Whenever Lang Tao makes

302
00:23:29,359 --> 00:23:30,720
large transactions,

303
00:23:31,359 --> 00:23:32,000
all the involved accounts

304
00:23:32,000 --> 00:23:33,319
will be investigated one by one.

305
00:23:34,759 --> 00:23:35,200
Good.

306
00:23:36,039 --> 00:23:36,440
How about this:

307
00:23:37,440 --> 00:23:39,880
your Task Force should go over the details again,

308
00:23:40,720 --> 00:23:41,720
and keep the information synchronized.

309
00:23:42,440 --> 00:23:43,039
Yes, sir.

310
00:23:46,640 --> 00:23:47,599
Who is Lang Tao?

311
00:23:48,640 --> 00:23:50,519
Read the file and see for yourself.

312
00:23:56,039 --> 00:23:58,000
The Political Department has set up a funeral committee.

313
00:23:58,920 --> 00:24:00,599
Arrange for Chief Zhao to go help out.

314
00:24:01,759 --> 00:24:02,200
Okay.

315
00:24:02,880 --> 00:24:04,279
We need a senior comrade at a time like this.

316
00:24:04,880 --> 00:24:06,119
Chief Zhao is a good fit.

317
00:24:06,559 --> 00:24:07,319
Besides,

318
00:24:07,400 --> 00:24:08,640
we will cooperate with the Political Department

319
00:24:09,000 --> 00:24:11,440
to hold a memorial service for Lu Zhong.

320
00:24:11,920 --> 00:24:12,680
Let's make it a high-profile one.

321
00:24:13,000 --> 00:24:14,160
So he can leave with honor.

322
00:24:15,359 --> 00:24:16,559
After all, he's gone.

323
00:24:18,119 --> 00:24:19,799
We'll fight for every honor we can get him.

324
00:24:20,720 --> 00:24:22,480
It's the least we, the living, can do.

325
00:24:25,359 --> 00:24:26,039
Also, over the next two days,

326
00:24:26,039 --> 00:24:27,720
think about the memorial service's

327
00:24:28,319 --> 00:24:29,680
eulogies and speeches.

328
00:24:29,960 --> 00:24:30,880
You will be the one writing them.

329
00:24:31,720 --> 00:24:33,039
Understood. Rest assured.

330
00:24:33,240 --> 00:24:33,599
Chief Guo,

331
00:24:34,680 --> 00:24:35,960
about our Hongye police officers'

332
00:24:35,960 --> 00:24:37,240
putting duty above family and risking their lives,

333
00:24:37,240 --> 00:24:38,359
and their spirit of serving the people...

334
00:24:38,519 --> 00:24:39,119
True enough.

335
00:24:39,240 --> 00:24:40,359
But let's be more practical,

336
00:24:40,440 --> 00:24:41,559
so that the higher-ups

337
00:24:42,000 --> 00:24:43,519
can see the hardships of our frontline officers.

338
00:24:44,519 --> 00:24:44,960
Understood.

339
00:24:48,200 --> 00:24:49,680
Right, what did you want to report to me?

340
00:24:53,400 --> 00:24:54,359
I just wanted to report in advance

341
00:24:54,920 --> 00:24:56,079
that Comrade Lu Zhong's memorial service

342
00:24:56,359 --> 00:24:57,200
will be a complete success.

343
00:25:13,960 --> 00:25:14,319
Chief.

344
00:25:15,079 --> 00:25:15,640
About this...

345
00:25:15,720 --> 00:25:17,359
Print 1,000 more copies of Jin Yonggang's Wanted Notice.

346
00:25:17,480 --> 00:25:17,759
Is that enough?

347
00:25:18,200 --> 00:25:18,920
It's enough for now.

348
00:25:19,359 --> 00:25:21,119
Have the patrol officers carry a few extra copies.

349
00:25:21,359 --> 00:25:22,680
Hand them out in crowded areas.

350
00:25:22,799 --> 00:25:23,079
Got it.

351
00:25:23,079 --> 00:25:24,039
And the neighborhood committees.

352
00:25:24,160 --> 00:25:25,599
Make sure every street organization gets them.

353
00:25:25,599 --> 00:25:25,839
Consider it done.

354
00:25:25,839 --> 00:25:27,160
Mobilize the public to gather leads.

355
00:25:27,839 --> 00:25:28,160
I'm on it.

356
00:25:28,400 --> 00:25:28,720
Also,

357
00:25:29,039 --> 00:25:30,440
send two men over to Mr. Jin's place.

358
00:25:31,000 --> 00:25:31,799
Chief, I already did.

359
00:25:32,319 --> 00:25:33,240
They got kicked out.

360
00:25:34,200 --> 00:25:34,720
Kicked out?

361
00:25:35,720 --> 00:25:37,799
Narcotics and CID...

362
00:25:38,119 --> 00:25:39,000
They already stationed plainclothes there.

363
00:25:39,440 --> 00:25:40,559
Watching the place 24/7.

364
00:25:41,119 --> 00:25:42,240
They think we're not professional enough.

365
00:25:42,480 --> 00:25:44,000
Told us to stay out of their way and do our own jobs.

366
00:25:44,960 --> 00:25:45,519
Just get back to work.

367
00:26:20,279 --> 00:26:21,039
Guys,

368
00:26:21,799 --> 00:26:22,960
for Lu Zhong's memorial service,

369
00:26:23,200 --> 00:26:25,480
I want everyone who knew him

370
00:26:25,880 --> 00:26:27,319
to write a few words.

371
00:26:28,440 --> 00:26:29,319
Give it some thought.

372
00:26:38,160 --> 00:26:40,319
A hero of blood and fire.

373
00:26:41,079 --> 00:26:42,279
Fearless of death.

374
00:26:43,759 --> 00:26:44,880
He knew the people and the streets.

375
00:26:51,119 --> 00:26:51,559
All filled out.

376
00:26:53,039 --> 00:26:53,559
Thanks.

377
00:27:00,200 --> 00:27:00,920
It really is you.

378
00:27:01,359 --> 00:27:02,240
Chief Ji.

379
00:27:02,599 --> 00:27:03,279
What brings you here?

380
00:27:05,400 --> 00:27:06,200
Getting a replacement ID.

381
00:27:06,559 --> 00:27:07,880
We'll mail it to you within seven business days.

382
00:27:07,880 --> 00:27:08,519
Postage on delivery.

383
00:27:08,519 --> 00:27:09,920
Please confirm this mailing address.

384
00:27:14,000 --> 00:27:14,640
No problem.

385
00:27:16,960 --> 00:27:18,160
You don't live around Old Street anymore?

386
00:27:19,039 --> 00:27:20,720
Yeah. That place is just too rough.

387
00:27:55,920 --> 00:27:57,480
Gangzi messed with things he shouldn't have.

388
00:27:58,039 --> 00:27:59,920
The police arrested him to save him.

389
00:28:00,640 --> 00:28:03,319
As long as he never touches that stuff again,

390
00:28:03,880 --> 00:28:04,599
he'll definitely be fine.

391
00:28:48,599 --> 00:28:49,880
About that address you mentioned,

392
00:28:50,440 --> 00:28:51,359
we went there.

393
00:28:52,279 --> 00:28:53,240
No one was there.

394
00:28:54,920 --> 00:28:57,960
Find him and hand him over to us.

395
00:28:59,000 --> 00:28:59,880
Or else,

396
00:29:00,640 --> 00:29:02,640
your dad is a dead man.

397
00:29:16,200 --> 00:29:16,599
Chief Ji.

398
00:29:17,240 --> 00:29:19,079
See if this is the guy you're looking for.

399
00:29:19,920 --> 00:29:21,559
The back of his head looks just like him.

400
00:29:23,359 --> 00:29:26,000
Th-This is the street by the market, right?

401
00:29:26,759 --> 00:29:29,119
Yes, yes, yes. I'm following him right now.

402
00:29:29,559 --> 00:29:29,799
Alright.

403
00:29:30,319 --> 00:29:32,119
Auntie Liu, be careful.

404
00:29:32,119 --> 00:29:33,119
We're heading over there now.

405
00:29:33,960 --> 00:29:34,920
Auntie Liu, I... I mean...

406
00:29:36,079 --> 00:29:37,519
Chief, searching like this is too unreliable.

407
00:29:37,559 --> 00:29:38,480
It feels like a joke.

408
00:29:38,880 --> 00:29:40,039
We're guessing from the back of a head.

409
00:29:40,039 --> 00:29:41,279
Next, we'll be doing face readings.

410
00:29:41,319 --> 00:29:42,279
Never mind if it's true or not.

411
00:29:42,279 --> 00:29:43,279
If there's a lead, we investigate.

412
00:29:43,599 --> 00:29:44,440
This is a bit more reliable.

413
00:29:44,640 --> 00:29:45,519
At least we have a view of his back.

414
00:29:45,799 --> 00:29:46,880
Attention, everyone.

415
00:29:47,279 --> 00:29:48,519
We have a lead on Jin Yonggang.

416
00:29:48,920 --> 00:29:50,359
Anyone in the station not on an assignment,

417
00:29:50,400 --> 00:29:52,039
grab your gear and head to the pedestrian street.

418
00:29:52,240 --> 00:29:52,720
Hurry up.

419
00:29:53,079 --> 00:29:53,599
Chief Ji.

420
00:29:53,759 --> 00:29:54,920
Should we notify the City Bureau?

421
00:29:56,359 --> 00:29:57,480
Let's confirm it's him first.

422
00:29:57,680 --> 00:29:58,720
Let's not come up empty again.

423
00:29:59,160 --> 00:30:00,160
Let's move, let's move!

424
00:30:33,200 --> 00:30:34,039
Look, the one eating over there.

425
00:30:34,039 --> 00:30:35,119
The guy in the hat, that's him.

426
00:30:36,880 --> 00:30:37,640
Thank you, Auntie Liu.

427
00:30:46,640 --> 00:30:47,119
It's him.

428
00:30:48,400 --> 00:30:49,400
Xiaobai, notify the Municipal Bureau.

429
00:30:50,519 --> 00:30:51,119
Do we move in?

430
00:30:52,200 --> 00:30:52,839
It's too crowded here.

431
00:30:53,480 --> 00:30:54,400
He might have a gun on him.

432
00:30:54,920 --> 00:30:55,599
We'll follow him.

433
00:30:56,519 --> 00:30:58,319
And make the arrest somewhere less crowded.

434
00:31:01,880 --> 00:31:02,680
Everyone, put on a jacket.

435
00:32:11,680 --> 00:32:12,319
What are you doing?!

436
00:32:12,319 --> 00:32:13,160
Help!

437
00:32:13,200 --> 00:32:14,160
Let go! Don't scream!

438
00:32:14,160 --> 00:32:14,960
Scream again and I'll kill you!

439
00:32:15,640 --> 00:32:17,200
Gangzi, what are you doing?

440
00:32:17,240 --> 00:32:17,960
Put the knife down.

441
00:32:17,960 --> 00:32:18,359
Sis.

442
00:32:18,799 --> 00:32:19,559
Let me go, okay?

443
00:32:19,559 --> 00:32:20,799
Put the knife down, do you hear me?!

444
00:32:20,799 --> 00:32:21,240
Get back.

445
00:32:21,440 --> 00:32:22,240
Step back.

446
00:32:44,799 --> 00:32:46,759
I wonder if we'll see any action today.

447
00:32:57,599 --> 00:32:59,759
You haven't used this sniper in real combat yet, right?

448
00:33:00,880 --> 00:33:02,200
Check if the bolt works smoothly.

449
00:33:03,359 --> 00:33:04,359
Step out and give it a try.

450
00:33:11,640 --> 00:33:13,680
Hello, is Chief Ji around?

451
00:33:15,039 --> 00:33:15,640
It's Tan Yan.

452
00:33:17,799 --> 00:33:18,279
Hello.

453
00:33:19,759 --> 00:33:21,160
She hasn't been answering my calls.

454
00:33:21,480 --> 00:33:22,240
Is she not at the station?

455
00:33:24,640 --> 00:33:25,519
She went to provide backup.

456
00:33:25,880 --> 00:33:26,640
What is it?

457
00:33:31,000 --> 00:33:31,440
Gangzi,

458
00:33:31,720 --> 00:33:32,799
put the knife down, okay?

459
00:33:32,799 --> 00:33:33,359
Step back!

460
00:33:33,359 --> 00:33:34,160
Everyone step back!

461
00:33:34,160 --> 00:33:35,039
It's not too late to turn yourself in.

462
00:33:35,039 --> 00:33:36,279
Go ahead. Yes, I know. I know.

463
00:33:37,359 --> 00:33:38,599
Okay, I have to hang up now.

464
00:33:38,759 --> 00:33:39,839
Alright, that's it for now. Thanks.

465
00:33:39,839 --> 00:33:40,920
All units, get in position ASAP.

466
00:33:41,200 --> 00:33:41,960
Get in position ASAP.

467
00:33:42,440 --> 00:33:43,240
Captain Zhang, Captain Na.

468
00:33:43,400 --> 00:33:43,920
What's the situation?

469
00:33:44,960 --> 00:33:45,880
Jin Yonggang is inside.

470
00:33:45,880 --> 00:33:47,200
He's holding a mother and son hostage.

471
00:33:47,559 --> 00:33:48,680
He's extremely agitated right now.

472
00:33:48,839 --> 00:33:49,480
He won't let us come any closer.

473
00:33:49,480 --> 00:33:50,480
Our chief is negotiating with him.

474
00:33:50,839 --> 00:33:52,119
Is she wearing a bodycam?

475
00:33:52,119 --> 00:33:52,519
Yes, she is.

476
00:33:53,079 --> 00:33:53,880
Here, send the signal.

477
00:33:54,039 --> 00:33:54,720
Send the signal! Send it!

478
00:33:54,720 --> 00:33:55,279
Hurry, hurry!

479
00:34:04,440 --> 00:34:05,519
Chief Ji is currently in there

480
00:34:05,599 --> 00:34:06,359
talking with them.

481
00:34:07,359 --> 00:34:08,360
Don't spook him!

482
00:34:13,679 --> 00:34:14,280
Lu Xiao,

483
00:34:14,280 --> 00:34:15,960
lead a team and move in covertly from both sides.

484
00:34:16,559 --> 00:34:17,800
Bo Jiani, find a sniper position.

485
00:34:17,960 --> 00:34:19,280
The rest of you, get ready for Rappelling with me.

486
00:34:20,000 --> 00:34:20,400
Captain Liao.

487
00:34:21,320 --> 00:34:22,519
The suspect is linked to the "Spring Snow" case.

488
00:34:23,639 --> 00:34:24,599
Try not to open fire, okay?

489
00:34:26,119 --> 00:34:27,760
As long as the hostages are not threatened,

490
00:34:28,079 --> 00:34:28,719
we can hold our fire.

491
00:34:29,519 --> 00:34:30,000
Move!

492
00:34:30,159 --> 00:34:30,639
Yes, sir!

493
00:34:43,719 --> 00:34:44,599
Sniper in position.

494
00:34:45,199 --> 00:34:47,039
Gangzi, put the knife down first.

495
00:34:47,760 --> 00:34:48,559
Trust me.

496
00:34:49,199 --> 00:34:50,480
I won't hurt you, Gangzi.

497
00:34:50,920 --> 00:34:52,880
What do you want? Who do you want to see?

498
00:34:53,239 --> 00:34:54,840
Tell me, I'll arrange it for you.

499
00:34:55,000 --> 00:34:55,639
Okay, Gangzi?

500
00:34:56,400 --> 00:34:56,960
Get out!

501
00:34:57,880 --> 00:34:58,280
Gangzi.

502
00:34:59,039 --> 00:35:01,159
Sis, don't push me, okay?

503
00:35:01,840 --> 00:35:03,079
If you come closer, I'll kill her right now!

504
00:35:03,440 --> 00:35:04,239
Gangzi! Gangzi!

505
00:35:04,239 --> 00:35:04,519
Chief Guo.

506
00:35:04,519 --> 00:35:04,920
Listen to me.

507
00:35:05,320 --> 00:35:05,800
Chief Guo.

508
00:35:05,840 --> 00:35:06,239
Chief Guo.

509
00:35:07,079 --> 00:35:07,639
What's the situation?

510
00:35:07,840 --> 00:35:08,920
Chief Ji is inside talking to him.

511
00:35:09,000 --> 00:35:10,119
SWAT is already in position.

512
00:35:11,559 --> 00:35:13,320
This is the feed from the bodycam.

513
00:35:14,280 --> 00:35:16,360
Gangzi, put the knife down, okay?

514
00:35:18,280 --> 00:35:19,199
If we breach,

515
00:35:20,159 --> 00:35:21,360
can we guarantee the hostage's safety?

516
00:35:22,599 --> 00:35:24,960
Right now, Jin Yonggang is highly unstable.

517
00:35:25,159 --> 00:35:27,039
Not to mention he's connected to the Lu Zhong case.

518
00:35:27,239 --> 00:35:28,239
If we breach now,

519
00:35:29,079 --> 00:35:29,719
we can't guarantee it.

520
00:35:30,480 --> 00:35:31,360
Where are Liao Bufan and his team?

521
00:35:31,719 --> 00:35:32,440
They are already in position.

522
00:35:34,280 --> 00:35:35,199
Gangzi. Gangzi.

523
00:35:35,679 --> 00:35:36,920
Do you remember back in elementary school,

524
00:35:37,360 --> 00:35:38,480
when some kids bullied you?

525
00:35:38,599 --> 00:35:39,400
I saw it happen.

526
00:35:39,800 --> 00:35:41,840
We teamed up and beat them up.

527
00:35:43,159 --> 00:35:44,119
Later, your dad found out,

528
00:35:44,559 --> 00:35:45,559
and beat you up again.

529
00:35:46,239 --> 00:35:47,840
He took us to apologize to them.

530
00:35:48,559 --> 00:35:49,360
Remember, Gangzi?

531
00:35:51,840 --> 00:35:52,280
I remember.

532
00:35:54,159 --> 00:35:54,800
After we apologized,

533
00:35:56,039 --> 00:35:57,199
we beat them up again.

534
00:35:58,920 --> 00:36:01,239
Yeah. I couldn't stand my brother getting bullied.

535
00:36:01,880 --> 00:36:03,800
So I had to settle the score.

536
00:36:05,400 --> 00:36:05,880
Gangzi.

537
00:36:07,199 --> 00:36:08,239
I treat you like my own brother.

538
00:36:09,159 --> 00:36:10,360
And you treat me like a sister, right?

539
00:36:11,880 --> 00:36:12,400
Gangzi.

540
00:36:13,719 --> 00:36:14,599
Do you trust me?

541
00:36:16,519 --> 00:36:16,960
Sis...

542
00:36:18,199 --> 00:36:18,960
I trust you.

543
00:36:20,719 --> 00:36:21,800
But I don't trust the police.

544
00:36:39,719 --> 00:36:40,559
Lao Tan! Lao Tan!

545
00:36:40,880 --> 00:36:41,840
Lao Tan! Lao Tan, come back!

546
00:36:43,400 --> 00:36:44,639
I promise to get you out alive.

547
00:36:45,079 --> 00:36:45,480
Okay?

548
00:36:45,559 --> 00:36:46,760
Let me talk to him. Let me talk to him.

549
00:36:47,199 --> 00:36:48,400
Gangzi. I'm Tan Yan.

550
00:36:49,159 --> 00:36:50,400
Let me break this down for you, okay?

551
00:36:51,280 --> 00:36:51,760
Look,

552
00:36:52,440 --> 00:36:54,880
the scariest, hardest part right now

553
00:36:55,639 --> 00:36:57,079
isn't the problem you're facing.

554
00:36:57,840 --> 00:36:59,199
It's that you took this wrong step,

555
00:36:59,480 --> 00:37:00,440
and now there's no turning back.

556
00:37:01,480 --> 00:37:02,199
Why are you doing this?

557
00:37:02,599 --> 00:37:04,360
You... You're holding a knife to someone else's throat,

558
00:37:04,360 --> 00:37:05,639
but you're actually holding it to your own.

559
00:37:05,639 --> 00:37:06,480
Think about it.

560
00:37:07,440 --> 00:37:08,079
Isn't that right?

561
00:37:10,280 --> 00:37:11,119
You need some breathing room.

562
00:37:12,920 --> 00:37:14,000
Whether it's for yourself,

563
00:37:14,800 --> 00:37:16,480
or for Mr. Jin.

564
00:37:18,079 --> 00:37:18,800
Put the knife down.

565
00:37:20,000 --> 00:37:20,599
Let the hostage go.

566
00:37:21,440 --> 00:37:23,039
If you need a hostage, take me.

567
00:37:23,440 --> 00:37:24,079
It's the safest bet.

568
00:37:25,159 --> 00:37:26,360
I sit in an office all day.

569
00:37:26,639 --> 00:37:27,440
I'm just a pen-pusher.

570
00:37:28,159 --> 00:37:29,800
I just write reports and attend meetings.

571
00:37:30,480 --> 00:37:32,639
I get dizzy if I stand for too long.

572
00:37:34,119 --> 00:37:34,599
You know?

573
00:37:35,199 --> 00:37:36,119
Taking me is your safest bet.

574
00:37:36,599 --> 00:37:37,239
I don't believe you!

575
00:37:37,920 --> 00:37:38,920
Gangzi, trust me.

576
00:37:38,920 --> 00:37:40,000
I don't trust anyone!

577
00:37:40,119 --> 00:37:41,039
Don't push me.

578
00:37:41,039 --> 00:37:42,280
Push me again, and I'll kill her right now!

579
00:37:43,239 --> 00:37:44,079
The suspect is being very cautious.

580
00:37:44,599 --> 00:37:45,880
I can't find a clear shot.

581
00:37:46,159 --> 00:37:47,239
Gangzi, listen to me.

582
00:37:48,119 --> 00:37:49,239
We won't push you. We won't.

583
00:37:50,920 --> 00:37:52,159
Let's talk this out, okay?

584
00:37:52,320 --> 00:37:53,440
It's fine if you don't trust her.

585
00:37:54,199 --> 00:37:55,280
She's just from a local precinct.

586
00:37:55,639 --> 00:37:56,400
But you can trust me.

587
00:37:57,519 --> 00:37:58,360
I'm from the Municipal Bureau.

588
00:37:59,119 --> 00:37:59,920
Look at my rank.

589
00:38:00,280 --> 00:38:01,039
I've got two stars.

590
00:38:02,400 --> 00:38:03,039
She only has one.

591
00:38:03,840 --> 00:38:04,760
My rank is higher than hers.

592
00:38:06,280 --> 00:38:07,159
I promise you,

593
00:38:08,280 --> 00:38:08,800
you'll be fine.

594
00:38:10,920 --> 00:38:11,360
Really.

595
00:38:12,400 --> 00:38:13,280
You can't lie to me.

596
00:38:14,679 --> 00:38:15,559
None of you can lie to me!

597
00:38:15,559 --> 00:38:16,440
She and I won't lie to you.

598
00:38:17,079 --> 00:38:17,519
Gangzi.

599
00:38:19,320 --> 00:38:20,280
I promise you'll be fine.

600
00:38:35,880 --> 00:38:37,519
Target is at a suitable sniper angle.

601
00:38:37,639 --> 00:38:38,920
Should I take the shot? Please advise.

602
00:38:41,119 --> 00:38:42,480
Hold your fire. Wait for an opening.

603
00:38:46,199 --> 00:38:46,920
The hostage is in danger.

604
00:38:47,199 --> 00:38:48,039
I don't have a clear shot.

605
00:38:48,920 --> 00:38:50,079
Move again and I'll kill you!

606
00:38:50,079 --> 00:38:51,719
Gangzi, think about Mr. Jin.

607
00:38:51,960 --> 00:38:52,880
Don't make things any worse.

608
00:38:52,880 --> 00:38:55,000
Gangzi, put down the knife.

609
00:38:55,280 --> 00:38:56,480
You need to calm down.

610
00:38:56,519 --> 00:38:58,360
Cannot lock onto the suspect. Please advise.

611
00:38:58,480 --> 00:39:00,800
We must ensure the hostage's safety.

612
00:40:03,840 --> 00:40:04,400
The suspect is dead.

613
00:40:30,599 --> 00:40:31,840
When I was in fifth grade,

614
00:40:32,599 --> 00:40:33,559
Gangzi was in third grade.

615
00:40:36,440 --> 00:40:38,039
My parents were busy with work back then,

616
00:40:39,360 --> 00:40:41,079
so Mr. Jin would have me over for dinner.

617
00:40:43,360 --> 00:40:44,400
Every time I went over,

618
00:40:45,280 --> 00:40:46,679
he'd make lots of delicious food for me.

619
00:40:49,599 --> 00:40:50,360
Mr. Jin said

620
00:40:50,840 --> 00:40:52,840
his biggest regret in life was

621
00:40:54,039 --> 00:40:55,079
not having a daughter.

622
00:40:58,280 --> 00:40:59,760
He treated me like his own daughter,

623
00:41:01,679 --> 00:41:03,159
and I treated Gangzi like my own brother.

624
00:41:06,440 --> 00:41:07,679
When Mr. Jin first got sick,

625
00:41:09,679 --> 00:41:10,800
he would always hold my hand

626
00:41:12,199 --> 00:41:14,400
and beg me to take good care of his son.

627
00:41:17,000 --> 00:41:18,599
He didn't expect Gangzi to achieve great things.

628
00:41:20,519 --> 00:41:22,159
He just hoped I could keep him in line,

629
00:41:23,880 --> 00:41:24,880
keep him on the right path,

630
00:41:26,599 --> 00:41:27,960
so he could live a safe and peaceful life.

631
00:41:33,679 --> 00:41:35,599
I saw Mr. Jin at the scene today.

632
00:41:37,320 --> 00:41:38,159
He saw everything.

633
00:41:40,719 --> 00:41:41,440
I don't know...

634
00:41:45,440 --> 00:41:46,719
I promised Mr. Jin

635
00:41:48,280 --> 00:41:49,519
I would take good care of Gangzi.

636
00:41:53,440 --> 00:41:54,719
How am I supposed to explain this to him?

637
00:43:12,199 --> 00:43:13,400
Did you have to go for a headshot?

638
00:43:13,480 --> 00:43:14,639
If I had to do it again, I'd do the same thing.

639
00:43:14,639 --> 00:43:15,440
What do you mean "again"?

640
00:43:15,440 --> 00:43:16,360
You're really pushing it, aren't you?

641
00:43:16,400 --> 00:43:16,840
What do you mean I'm pushing it?

642
00:43:16,880 --> 00:43:18,000
You know what a police officer's duty is,

643
00:43:18,000 --> 00:43:18,840
don't you?

644
00:43:18,840 --> 00:43:19,920
Given the situation at the time,

645
00:43:20,000 --> 00:43:21,480
Liao Bufan's actions were completely justified.

646
00:43:21,559 --> 00:43:22,840
I'm planning to do

647
00:43:22,840 --> 00:43:24,480
an exclusive interview with you.

648
00:43:24,639 --> 00:43:25,320
I won't give a statement.

649
00:43:25,800 --> 00:43:27,079
This situation right now

650
00:43:28,039 --> 00:43:28,760
is way too big.

651
00:43:30,280 --> 00:43:32,079
Help us look for that woman again.

652
00:43:32,519 --> 00:43:33,760
No matter where I go now,

653
00:43:34,400 --> 00:43:35,559
I just don't feel safe.
